{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vVHZfU2hvd3MvRW5nbGlzaC8yMDI2L1RoZSUyMFdlc3RpZXMlMjAlMjgyMDI2JTI5Lw","type":"series","name":"The Westies","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/6nNxw6SsbEtSpktVEGdoYDqPH7C.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/tT2MwxaST3Fx1Dg4u9v82sDrIu.jpg","description":"As the Javits Center construction project ignites a battle for profit in early 1980s Hell's Kitchen, a generational rift threatens the uneasy peace between violent Irish gang the Westies and the Mafia, and draws FBI heat.\n\nRated TV-MA · Returning Series · First aired 12 Jul 2026 · United States of America · Language: English\nStudio: Chris Brancato, MGM+ Studios · Network: MGM+\n\nComplete series. On your server: S1 8/8\n\nOn your server — Audio: English","releaseInfo":"2026","genres":["Drama","Crime","English"],"videos":[{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vVHZfU2hvd3MvRW5nbGlzaC8yMDI2L1RoZSUyMFdlc3RpZXMlMjAlMjgyMDI2JTI5Lw.1.1","title":"The Troubles","season":1,"episode":1,"released":"2026-07-12T00:00:00.000Z","overview":"The Westies' fragile deal with the Italians unravels after a reckless kidnapping. Flanagan is released from Bellevue and rejoins Roarke's crew, Keenan is pulled onto an FBI task force, and Bridget receives a dangerous assignment from an old IRA contact.","thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/o0z4gcI4VB9PWek8BAY0eREmr4.jpg"},{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vVHZfU2hvd3MvRW5nbGlzaC8yMDI2L1RoZSUyMFdlc3RpZXMlMjAlMjgyMDI2JTI5Lw.1.2","title":"The Houdini","season":1,"episode":2,"released":"2026-07-12T00:00:00.000Z","overview":"Roarke and the Westies hide the body of a dead Italian mobster and stage crimes to cover up the murder before Gotti retaliates. Polk pressures Keenan to dig into Sweeney's Mafia ties, while Bridget uncovers more of Cahill's plot.","thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/85govEmGpVS5e37idn63AiQ6Lu8.jpg"},{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vVHZfU2hvd3MvRW5nbGlzaC8yMDI2L1RoZSUyMFdlc3RpZXMlMjAlMjgyMDI2JTI5Lw.1.3","title":"The Starship","season":1,"episode":3,"released":"2026-07-19T00:00:00.000Z","overview":"Sweeney strikes a deal with Castellano: rob a Colombian disco and Flanagan walks free. Bridget seeks counsel about Cahill, while Keenan investigates the killing of a cop in Boston.","thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/eaaNwAwKnYkBmAvYOOJTxKTykTr.jpg"},{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vVHZfU2hvd3MvRW5nbGlzaC8yMDI2L1RoZSUyMFdlc3RpZXMlMjAlMjgyMDI2JTI5Lw.1.4","title":"Favors and Funerals","season":1,"episode":4,"released":"2026-07-26T00:00:00.000Z","overview":"Roarke clashes with Sweeney over selling stolen cocaine, but Sweeney has his own agenda. As he receives a Hibernian Society award, Gotti orders a hit. Bridget learns Cahill's target is someone from her past. Keenan struggles to help his son.","thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/jku8rIieWlgQ7Ydf7Fn4qfARpEy.jpg"},{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vVHZfU2hvd3MvRW5nbGlzaC8yMDI2L1RoZSUyMFdlc3RpZXMlMjAlMjgyMDI2JTI5Lw.1.5","title":"A Right Rose Tree","season":1,"episode":5,"released":"2026-08-02T00:00:00.000Z","overview":"Sweeney lets Roarke sell cocaine only if he sources it himself, putting him in Gotti's crosshairs as Gotti suspects the Westies are defying Castellano. Bridget helps Cahill secure new explosives for their IRA plot. Polk pressures Keenan to wear a wire.","thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/2YIjYTSwGOaqkiDjrp9iexUeMgF.jpg"},{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vVHZfU2hvd3MvRW5nbGlzaC8yMDI2L1RoZSUyMFdlc3RpZXMlMjAlMjgyMDI2JTI5Lw.1.6","title":"Rad Tad","season":1,"episode":6,"released":"2026-08-09T00:00:00.000Z","overview":"Roarke gets a risky loan from Ruby Stein to fund a cocaine deal with a silver-spooned hotshot from downtown, only for the deal to implode. Keenan targets an older Westie to pressure Sweeney, while Bridget and the IRA cell move on Colonel Markham.","thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/zDLEBhdDtLRGqtQuPp2HZIcdNy3.jpg"},{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vVHZfU2hvd3MvRW5nbGlzaC8yMDI2L1RoZSUyMFdlc3RpZXMlMjAlMjgyMDI2JTI5Lw.1.7","title":"A Boy Made of Trouble","season":1,"episode":7,"released":"2026-08-16T00:00:00.000Z","overview":"Roarke gets a risky loan from Ruby Stein to fund a cocaine deal with a silver-spooned hotshot from downtown, only for the deal to implode. Keenan targets an older Westie to pressure Sweeney, while Bridget and the IRA cell move on Colonel Markham.","thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/vIxhkFcQbz1vswVnju53KHPCKrL.jpg"},{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vVHZfU2hvd3MvRW5nbGlzaC8yMDI2L1RoZSUyMFdlc3RpZXMlMjAlMjgyMDI2JTI5Lw.1.8","title":"The Irish Goodbye","season":1,"episode":8,"released":"2026-08-23T00:00:00.000Z","overview":"Roarke and Sweeney's fallout splits the Westies, pitting old guard against young. Bridget pushes ahead with the mission but faces shattering truths. Polk increases pressure on Sweeney and Gotti, while Keenan wrestles with guilt and a son slipping away.","thumbnail":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w300/cKmEpgXFugg3lvTNF6HVjgQiDZZ.jpg"}],"imdbRating":"7.4","cast":["J.K. Simmons","Titus Welliver","Tom Brittney","Stanley Morgan","Sarah Bolger","Jessica Frances Dukes","Hamish Allan-Headley","Vincent Walsh"],"director":["Chris Brancato","Michael Panes"],"released":"2026-07-12T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"F*ck those guys.","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Chris Brancato","character":"Director"},{"name":"J.K. Simmons","character":"Eamon Sweeney","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/ScmKoJ9eiSUOthAt1PDNLi8Fkw.jpg"},{"name":"Titus Welliver","character":"Glenn Keenan","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/3hTwn7Maktr6ONq1VvfqyRacjiv.jpg"},{"name":"Tom Brittney","character":"James 'Jimmy' Roarke","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/sUSd3jcC0wSoG6uH32p4SaeLLls.jpg"},{"name":"Stanley Morgan","character":"Mickey Flanagan","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p